el_nouns.json

Source: English Wiktionary, https://en.wiktionary.org/
Read through the MediaWiki API (https://en.wiktionary.org/w/api.php) on 2026-11-17, from the category members of
"Greek masculine nouns", "Greek feminine nouns", "Greek neuter nouns" and "Greek adjectives". The inflected forms come
from the Wiktextract dump of the English Wiktionary at kaikki.org
(https://kaikki.org/dictionary/Greek/kaikki.org-dictionary-Greek.jsonl), read on the same day. The category state and
the dump of that day are the source revision.

Attribution: Wiktionary contributors, the Greek noun and adjective entries of the English Wiktionary. The contributors
of each page are in its history at https://en.wiktionary.org/. Wiktextract, by Tatu Ylonen, extracts the forms.

Changes: the file keeps the lowercase forms of Greek letters, groups the forms of nouns and adjectives by gender and
case, leaves out the vocative, and leaves out the words of articles, pronouns, determiners, prepositions, conjunctions,
particles and contractions. scripts/extract_el_nouns.py makes the file.

it_noun_genders.json

Source: English Wiktionary, https://en.wiktionary.org/
Read through the MediaWiki API (https://en.wiktionary.org/w/api.php) on 2026-11-16, from the category
members of "Italian masculine nouns", "Italian feminine nouns", "Italian prepositions", "Italian conjunctions",
"Italian adverbs", "Italian pronouns", "Italian determiners" and "Italian articles". The category state of that
day is the source revision.

Attribution: Wiktionary contributors, "Italian masculine nouns" and "Italian feminine nouns", English Wiktionary.
The contributors of each page are in its history at https://en.wiktionary.org/.

Changes: the file keeps the lowercase words of two or more letters, lists the words of both gender categories
apart, and lists the words of the function-word categories. scripts/extract_noun_genders.py makes the file.

